// TEST: a block lambda whose open parameter is given a closed tuple takes it
// ============================================================================
// R10 remainder (the numbers-only rule, formalism 2.4): a block lambda's
// parameter its body leaves open is BOUND by a direct call's argument -- a Bool,
// a String, a struct, a sum-type value, an index value. A tuple argument was
// refused here (BL3001, "it would be compiled at a default numeric type"); since
// the floor round's F2 a CLOSED tuple (every component decided) binds the
// parameter as a struct does, and the body's projections take the components'
// types. A body that treats the tuple as a number is refused by the
// numbers-only rule (basic/600).
// ============================================================================
let r = {
    let idl = lambda(x) -> x
    idl((true, 1))
}
let p = r[1] + 1
// EXPECT: r = (true, 1)
// EXPECT: p = 2